  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Bird Song** (1 review): Bird Song ended with an abrupt stop, then moved into Bertha with a smoother transition, before Bird Song returned [5]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Greatest Story Ever Told**: rare: 12 archived performances [8]\n- **Mexicali Blues**: back after 91 archived shows (931 days); rare: 3 archived performances [8]\n- **Diamonds on the Soles of Her Shoes**: rare: 3 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadandco2018-06-09.nakamichi.flac24** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 173 min; rated 4.25/5 by 4 [1]\n- **deadandco2018-06-09.peluso.flac24**: source not stated; 18 songs; 173 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer felt the band sounded like a Dead cover band, with forced, slow playing and little fire, lacking earlier magic [6]\n- Reviewer says the magic came through strongly at about a dozen shows this tour; Raleigh shone less than Atlanta the previous night [7]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadandco2018-06-09.nakamichi.flac24**: taped by Chris Davis and George; transferred by Chris Davis and George; source: Nakamachi cm100/cp4 [Rainey/lawn/dfc] -> E.A.A. PSP-2 -> Tascam DR-680 [24/48] [1]\n- **deadandco2018-06-09.peluso.flac24**: taped by Chris Davis and George; transferred by Chris Davis; source: Peluso cemc6/ck4 [Rainey/lawn/dfc] -> BM2p+ UA-5 [digital] -> Tascam DR-680 [24/48] [2]",
